Third-party material

Software dependencies are listed in Cargo.lock; their licences are in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt
(`cargo xtask licences`), which the programs also carry (Help > About > Licences,
`solidcraft-cli licences`). The B-rep geometry kernel uses solidcore
(https://github.com/tangency-labs/solidcore), the pure-Rust port of NVIDIA's SMLib
from USD BRep, under the Apache License 2.0. Its pinned revision is in Cargo.toml;
its licence and NVIDIA attribution/NOTICE are included in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt.
SolidCraft accesses it through the safe Rust wrapper in crates/smlib.

Some code is adapted from sibling projects in the storytold family (CADCraft, GridCraft), which are
licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0; ATTRIBUTION.md lists the files.
The release packaging (.github/workflows/release.yml, packaging/) is adapted from PhotoCraft
(https://github.com/storytold/photocraft), licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

The incremental Radiance RGBE row adapter in crates/render/src/lighting/hdr.rs adapts
decoding state machines from image 0.25.10 (https://github.com/image-rs/image),
MIT OR Apache-2.0. ATTRIBUTION.md describes the bounded/cancellable changes; the
original licence texts are included in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt.

Most bundled assets are drawn in code or contributed originally; third-party fonts (Liberation Sans
for sketch text, BIZ UDPGothic for web Japanese display) are licensed under SIL OFL 1.1. The
per-file list is in ATTRIBUTION.md.

